This package bundles data from third parties, under their own licences:

1. GeoNames
   Files: src/jobradar/normalize/data/cities.tsv.gz (derived from cities15000 and countryInfo)
   Source: https://www.geonames.org/
   Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
   Changes: one row per city name or alternate name, with country, population, latitude and longitude.

2. LastRound AI ATS directory
   Files: rows with origin "lastround" in src/jobradar/defaults/ats_registry.csv.gz
   Source: https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/67239956 (figshare)
   Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
   Changes: only company board slugs that answered and listed at least one job open to Europe are kept;
   the vendor, slug and company name are re-checked against the live board.

3. open-jobs-data by ConorsCode
   Files: rows with origin "open_jobs_data" in src/jobradar/defaults/ats_registry.csv.gz
   Source: https://github.com/ConorsCode/open-jobs-data
   Licence: MIT License, Copyright (c) ConorsCode
   Changes: company board slugs only, filtered as above. The `open_jobs_data` source reads the
   project's published daily snapshot at run time; it is not bundled.

4. Common Crawl
   Files: rows with origin "commoncrawl" in src/jobradar/defaults/ats_registry.csv.gz
   Source: https://commoncrawl.org/ (URL index), used under the Common Crawl Terms of Use
   Changes: only public job-board URLs (vendor + company slug) were extracted from the index.

Recorded HTTP responses under tests/fixtures/ are copies of public job listings, kept only to test the
parsers offline. Job postings belong to the employers and boards that published them.
